Step 1: Register the application in Google Cloud Console
• Go to console.cloud.google.com, create a project (e.g. oauth-login-demo).
• APIs & Services -> OAuth consent screen: User type External, fill the app name and your email. While
the app is in Testing status, add your own Google account under Test users (only listed accounts can
log in).
• APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create Credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Application type: Web
application.
• Authorized redirect URIs (add both): http://localhost:8080/login/oauth2/code/google
(Spring Boot, browser login) and https://oauth.pstmn.io/v1/callback (Postman; use exactly
the Callback URL that Postman displays).
• Create, then copy the Client ID and Client secret.
